    "summary": "Blanket, composed of nine narrow strips of hand-spun white and black cotton, hand-sewn together along the selvedges. The warp is entirely of white cotton; the weft is also white but has supplementary weft threads in black. These form three pattern bands of continuous threads across the cloth, plus five small patterns of discontinuous black threads placed randomly across the surface. The warp ends have been left to form a fringe.",
